e d4 pawn: 2 attackers against 1 defender.","54…Qd3 joins the attack on the king and adds pressure on the d4 pawn.","White answers 55.Qe4."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"54…Qd3!! gives up the knight on c6 to stay in the game: after it Black holds the balance (0.00); anything else leaves Black losing (+3.47)."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"54…Qd3 leaves the knight on c6 hanging to the queen on d5. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If White takes the knight","text":"55.Qxc6 is met by 55…Qd2+. Then 56…Qd1+ gives check, and 57…Qe2+ gives check. Black is a piece down: Black holds the balance (0.00)."},{"title":"White's best try","text":"White's best is to leave the knight alone and play 55.Qe4. Black answers 55…Qd2+, and the queen on d3 gets away. Then 56…Qd1+ gives check, and 57…Qd2+ gives check. Material is level and Black holds the balance (0.00)."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 54…Nd8, is clearly weaker (+3.47 against 0.00). White answers 55.Bf8+. That would leave Black losing."}]},{"ply":110,"name":"55…Qd2+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"55…Qd2+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked queen to safety.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","The next best move, 55…Qxe4, would drop Black's winning chances from 49% to 35% (+1.68).","55…Qd2+ saves the attacked queen.","White answers 56.Kg3.","Engine line: 56.Kg3 Qc1 57.f4 Qg1+ 58.Qg2 Qe3+ (+0.05)."]},{"ply":114,"name":"57…Qd2+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"57…Qd2+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Gives check, so the reply is forced.","The next best move, 57…Kf7, would drop Black's winning chances from 49% to 16% (+4.43).","57…Qd2+ gives check.","White answers 58.Kg3.","Engine line: 58.Kg3 Qc1 59.Kg2 Qb2+ 60.Kh3 Qc1 (+0.03)."]},{"ply":116,"name":"58…Qc1","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"58…Qc1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the knight on c6, which was hanging.","The next best move, 58…Qd1, would drop Black's winning chances from 49% to 28% (+2.58).","58…Qc1 protects the knight on c6.","White answers 59.Kf2.","Engine line: 59.Kf2 Qd2+ 60.Kf1 Qd1+ 61.Kg2 Qd2+ (+0.12)."]},{"ply":124,"name":"62…Qd1","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"62…Qd1!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the knight on c6 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: White's best reply is 63.b4 Qf1 64.f4 gxf4+ instead (the engine rates it +0.02).","Attacks the b3 pawn, which is undefended.","62…Qd1 attacks the b3 pawn, which is undefended.","White answers 63.b4.","Engine line: 63.b4 Qf1 64.f4 gxf4+ 65.Qxf4 Qe1+ (+0.02)."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"62…Qd1!! leaves the knight on c6 hanging. Taking it still leaves Black level."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"The knight on c6 is attacked by the queen on e4, and 62…Qd1 doesn't save it. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If White takes the knight","text":"63.Qxc6 is met by 63…Qe1+. Then 64…Qe2+ gives check, and 65…Qf1+ gives check. Black is a piece down: Black holds the balance (0.00)."},{"title":"White's best try","text":"White's best is to leave the knight alone and play 63.b4. Black answers 63…Qf1, joining the attack on the king. Then 64…gxf4+ gives check, and 65…Qe1+ gives check. Black ends up a pawn ahead: Black holds the balance (+0.02)."}]},{"ply":146,"name":"73…Nd8","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"73…Nd8 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 46% to 8%.","points":["White answers 74.Bb6, which attacks the knight on d8, which is undefended.","The knight on d8 can be taken by the queen on e8.","Better was 73…Ne5 (+0.41): the knight joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the White king."],"better":"73…Ne5 gets the knight out of the way of Qxc6. Engine line: 74.Qe7+ Kg6 75.Qb7 Qe1+ 76.Bf2 Qh1 (+0.41)."},{"ply":151,"name":"76.Qe7+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"76.Qe7+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen forks the king and the knight: both can't be saved at once.","The queen joins the attack: it now hits 4 squares around the Black king.","The next best move, 76.Be3, would drop White's winning chances from 69% to 52% (+0.27).","76.Qe7+ forks the king and the knight.","Black answers 76…Nf7.","Engine line: 76…Nf7 77.Bc5 Qc8 78.b4 Kg6 79.Qf8 (+2.61)."]},{"ply":163,"name":"82.Qg6+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"82.Qg6+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen joins the attack: it now hits 4 squares around the Black king.","Adds a decisive attacker on the g5 pawn: 2 attackers against 1 defender.","The next best move, 82.Qe8+, would drop White's winning chances from 93% to 81% (+3.98).","82.Qg6+ joins the attack on the king and adds pressure on the g5 pawn.","It prepares Bg7+, with check: the queen covers g7.","Black answers 82…Kf8."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Indian Defense: Capablanca Variation","eco":"E16","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9.a3: 17 moves in all, 9 by White and 8 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9.a3: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}